WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Good to see John and Jan Feudo.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:04.860
They were traveling, made it back home safely.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:06.280
And so we thank the Lord for that.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.319
Be heading down to South Carolina on Tuesday,

00:00:08.319 --> 00:00:09.560
so you pray for them.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:10.800
And then once you pray for Brother Sammy,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:12.439
he's got a root canal on Wednesday.

00:00:12.439 --> 00:00:13.800
It was supposed to be on Friday.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.319
On Thursday night, we prayed.

00:00:15.319 --> 00:00:17.879
And it got changed to Wednesday.

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:19.959
And so you pray for him, if you will.

00:00:19.959 --> 00:00:21.479
And then also want to mention, Kim

00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:22.920
has been visiting with us.

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.799
She's been up here temporarily on a work assignment.

00:00:25.799 --> 00:00:27.760
And today is her last Sunday here.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:30.200
She'll be heading back home on Saturday.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.920
And so thank you for being with us

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.240
during these weeks of your travels.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.639
And if you come back to the Northern Virginia area,

00:00:37.639 --> 00:00:39.279
we'd certainly love to see you again.

00:00:39.279 --> 00:00:41.279
And so thank you for being with us.

00:00:41.279 --> 00:00:42.840
If you have your Bible with you this morning,

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.159
the book of James, James chapter number four.

00:00:46.159 --> 00:00:49.500
And we've been working through the book of James

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:52.959
this year during our morning services on Sunday morning.

00:00:52.959 --> 00:00:54.680
Our theme, of course, you see the banners.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:57.880
We sing the theme song, doers of the word.

00:00:57.880 --> 00:01:00.240
And we're reminded of that wonderful truth

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:02.560
as James says in James one in verse 22,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:05.279
but be doers of the word and not hearers only,

00:01:05.279 --> 00:01:07.480
deceiving your own selves.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:09.279
Last week in chapter number four,

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:12.000
we looked at verses 13 through 16.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.639
And we dealt with the subject matter

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:16.199
that your life is a vapor.

00:01:16.199 --> 00:01:17.239
Your life is a vapor.

00:01:17.239 --> 00:01:19.760
It appears for a little time and then it vanishes away.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:22.440
And we talked about the brevity of life

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.800
and what a reality that is for each and every one of us.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:29.720
And we recognize this morning the importance of that truth

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.019
and how we're to live day by day

00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:34.620
for the honor and glory of the Lord.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.800
We find that this fourth chapter of the book of James

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.639
concludes with a powerful principle.

00:01:39.639 --> 00:01:43.239
The last verse of chapter four will be the focus

00:01:43.239 --> 00:01:45.779
of our lesson, our message this morning.

00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:48.599
We've said this repeatedly that the content

00:01:48.599 --> 00:01:52.260
of the book of James is extremely practical.

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.580
And it deals with our daily living and how we take,

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.500
and that's why we find in chapter one

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.660
to be doers of the word.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.980
How do we take the principles and apply them in our lives?

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:03.819
And so we find as we look at this principle

00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:05.180
to end chapter number four,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:08.779
it really reveals to us the expectation,

00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:11.539
not only of James, but I would raise it a level

00:02:11.539 --> 00:02:15.419
and say it this way, the expectation of the Lord

00:02:15.419 --> 00:02:18.940
that we would take the instruction that's been given

00:02:19.059 --> 00:02:22.419
and that we would implement it into our lives.

00:02:22.419 --> 00:02:24.979
This is an expectation that God has

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:26.259
of every one of his people,

00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:28.860
that we would be doers of the word.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.399
In fact, the Lord Jesus Christ said,

00:02:30.399 --> 00:02:32.740
"'Why call ye me Lord, Lord,

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.940
"'and doest not the things that I say?'

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:38.139
We understand that he's our savior.

00:02:38.139 --> 00:02:40.539
We sang this morning multiple times

00:02:40.539 --> 00:02:42.580
about him being our savior.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:45.660
Hallelujah, what a savior was the last congregational song

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.979
that we sang this morning.

00:02:47.059 --> 00:02:50.139
He becomes my savior by recognizing the truth

00:02:50.139 --> 00:02:53.300
that he shed his blood for us on the cross of Calvary,

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:55.660
and we accept him as our personal savior.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:57.740
And hallelujah, what a savior.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.699
And we can say, I've been washed in the blood.

00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:02.419
And that's a glorious truth.

00:03:02.419 --> 00:03:05.139
And I'm thankful that he is my savior.

00:03:05.139 --> 00:03:07.179
And I hope this morning that each of you could say

00:03:07.179 --> 00:03:09.979
that he is your savior, but I want you to understand

00:03:09.979 --> 00:03:12.179
he wants to be the Lord of your life as well.

00:03:12.179 --> 00:03:14.699
He wants to be the master of your life.

00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:19.059
And so often there's a conflict that we face in our lives.

00:03:19.059 --> 00:03:21.100
And that conflict is simply this,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:24.860
I want to be the Lord, the master of my own life.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:27.820
And you wanna be the Lord, the master of your own life,

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.580
but he is Lord, he is savior.

00:03:30.580 --> 00:03:32.940
And I'm so thankful for that.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:37.539
And he, no doubt as we study through the scriptures,

00:03:37.539 --> 00:03:40.279
it is the expectation of the Lord

00:03:40.279 --> 00:03:43.699
that his people would implement the instruction

00:03:43.699 --> 00:03:45.660
that he's given to them in their lives.

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:47.380
In other words, that we would live

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.880
by the principles of God's word.

00:03:49.880 --> 00:03:51.699
As we look at verse 17, the Bible says,

00:03:51.699 --> 00:03:56.699
therefore, to him that knoweth to do good,

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:01.300
and doeth it not to him, it is sin.

00:04:02.699 --> 00:04:05.979
The word good, and we look here and we see that it says,

00:04:05.979 --> 00:04:08.460
therefore, to him that knoweth to do good,

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.660
that which is right, that which is noble,

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.979
that which is appropriate, that which is honorable.

00:04:13.979 --> 00:04:16.100
We would understand contextually

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:19.059
as we're dealing with it being God's word,

00:04:19.059 --> 00:04:21.299
but it's speaking about doing that which is good,

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:25.019
that which is acceptable in the sight of the Lord.

00:04:25.019 --> 00:04:28.500
And we find that as we look at this verse of scripture

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:31.579
and we find the conclusion to this fourth chapter,

00:04:31.579 --> 00:04:36.579
and he says, therefore, to him that knoweth to do good,

00:04:36.739 --> 00:04:41.739
and doeth it not to him, it is sin.

00:04:42.619 --> 00:04:44.420
Oftentimes, when we think about sin,

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:48.799
we think about the fact that evil acts are sin.

00:04:49.899 --> 00:04:54.579
And that's true, it's true, to do evil is sin.

00:04:54.579 --> 00:04:56.459
But we find here within the context

00:04:56.459 --> 00:05:01.239
of our passage this morning, to not do good is sin.

00:05:02.079 --> 00:05:06.000
To not do good, to know what is good

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.540
as we find here in the text, and to do it not to him,

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:10.380
it is sin.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.559
I want you to consider what Jeremiah said of Judah.

00:05:13.559 --> 00:05:17.600
The Lord is speaking, of course, to his people,

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:19.720
and he's using Jeremiah as the prophet.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.380
And in Jeremiah 4, in verse 22, it's not the entire verse,

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.359
but at the end of the verse, it says this,

00:05:24.359 --> 00:05:26.760
speaking of the people of Judah,

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:28.880
they are wise to do evil,

00:05:30.079 --> 00:05:33.059
but to do good, they have no knowledge.

00:05:34.019 --> 00:05:37.279
They are wise to do evil,

00:05:37.279 --> 00:05:40.440
but to do good, they have no knowledge.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.799
What a sad indictment that is.

00:05:43.839 --> 00:05:46.399
James here, in the book of James,

00:05:46.399 --> 00:05:48.920
he encourages his readers to do good,

00:05:48.920 --> 00:05:52.279
and reminds them that failing to do so is sin.

00:05:52.279 --> 00:05:54.200
I've simply entitled the message this morning,

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.799
do good, do good.

00:05:56.799 --> 00:05:57.959
As we look at the passage,

00:05:57.959 --> 00:05:59.959
let me just share a couple of thoughts with you.

00:05:59.959 --> 00:06:02.440
Number one, I want you to notice the revelation.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:06.040
The revelation, as we consider the verse of Scripture

00:06:06.040 --> 00:06:09.179
and this principle that closes this fourth chapter,

00:06:09.179 --> 00:06:11.760
the book of James, James says it this way,

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:16.559
therefore, notice, to him that knoweth to do good.

00:06:16.559 --> 00:06:18.239
The way that you know to do good

00:06:18.239 --> 00:06:20.200
is because it's been revealed to us.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.160
And we think about the revelation

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.239
as we'd consider this verse of Scripture,

00:06:24.239 --> 00:06:27.359
and we think about it in its immediate context.

00:06:27.359 --> 00:06:30.579
We understand that James is writing to these believers,

00:06:30.579 --> 00:06:32.839
and we've gone through the process

00:06:32.839 --> 00:06:34.839
over the course of this year,

00:06:34.839 --> 00:06:37.920
establishing the audience for the book of James,

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:42.299
and we understand that these immediate original recipients

00:06:42.299 --> 00:06:46.899
of the book of James, the immediate context of verse 17,

00:06:46.899 --> 00:06:50.559
is that they now have been given truth.

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:54.640
They now have been taught how they are to live.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.839
We might say it this way,

00:06:55.839 --> 00:06:58.440
they've been taught what they ought to do.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.799
And so therefore, they know some things.

00:07:00.799 --> 00:07:04.019
They're no longer ignorant about living.

00:07:04.019 --> 00:07:06.720
They understand that God has provided them

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:11.359
with clear instruction with regard to their daily behavior.

00:07:11.359 --> 00:07:13.279
Again, as we've mentioned,

00:07:13.279 --> 00:07:17.160
the fact that God has given to us in the book of James

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:19.119
such practical truth.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:22.480
Just the application in daily living.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.040
And so James, no doubt,

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:26.519
as we consider the revelation this morning,

00:07:26.519 --> 00:07:29.600
would have in his mind the immediate context

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.059
of that audience that he's writing to,

00:07:32.059 --> 00:07:33.880
that they know to do good.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:35.739
They've been told.

00:07:35.739 --> 00:07:39.839
And it's not that they were not informed.

00:07:39.839 --> 00:07:41.559
It's not that they were kept in the dark.

00:07:41.559 --> 00:07:45.119
No, the revelation has been given.

00:07:45.119 --> 00:07:46.880
But we understand this morning

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.600
that it's not simply the immediate context

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:52.200
of these first century believers,

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.299
these Jewish believers that receive the word of God.

00:07:55.299 --> 00:07:57.799
We find that there's a broader context

00:07:57.799 --> 00:08:00.839
that this principle really deals with.

00:08:00.839 --> 00:08:02.700
And that broader context would apply

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:04.720
to each one of us here this morning.

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:08.880
And that is that God has graciously given to us his word.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.440
I'm so thankful that we have a Bible.

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:14.359
Where would we be if we did not have a Bible?

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:16.579
I think about the period of the judges

00:08:17.279 --> 00:08:19.100
where every man did that which was right in his own sight.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.420
I think about the people in which we live in the midst of,

00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:25.540
and we find in various places around the globe today

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:27.260
that they do not have a Bible.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:30.179
Or even in a land like America where the Bible is available,

00:08:30.179 --> 00:08:33.179
but people have not submitted to the Bible.

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.460
They don't know the truth of God's word.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:38.619
And they live according to their own standards.

00:08:38.619 --> 00:08:40.940
They become their own standard.

00:08:40.940 --> 00:08:43.140
And we find that here,

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.500
as we would consider the broader context

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.380
of this principle in James four and verse 17,

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.179
God has graciously given to you,

00:08:51.179 --> 00:08:55.479
and God has graciously given to me the word of God.

00:08:55.479 --> 00:08:58.179
And what a tremendous blessing it is

00:08:58.179 --> 00:09:01.840
that we can gather together on a regular basis,

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:05.099
and we can open up the precious word of God,

00:09:05.099 --> 00:09:06.739
and we can have confidence

00:09:06.739 --> 00:09:09.460
because of the truth of preservation

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:13.260
that God, all scripture is given by inspiration of God.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.619
But we understand that God

00:09:14.619 --> 00:09:17.380
has providentially preserved his word,

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:21.900
and we can have 100% confidence in the word of God

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.700
this morning that we hold in our hands

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:25.340
that thus saith the Lord,

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:30.340
and God has given to us by revelation that which is good,

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:33.419
that which is appropriate, that which is honorable,

00:09:33.419 --> 00:09:36.340
that which is acceptable in his sight.

00:09:36.340 --> 00:09:39.619
And we find that as we look at this passage of scripture,

00:09:39.619 --> 00:09:41.760
and we consider the context,

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:43.719
and we understand what's going on,

00:09:43.719 --> 00:09:45.960
this morning we must acknowledge

00:09:45.960 --> 00:09:49.400
that God has given to me the Bible.

00:09:50.799 --> 00:09:53.039
And therefore, I'm accountable.

00:09:54.119 --> 00:09:57.200
To whom much is given, much is required.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:10:00.039
We understand this morning that the...

00:10:00.039 --> 00:10:03.239
Bible teaches us that man is without excuse.

00:10:03.239 --> 00:10:04.879
Why is man without excuse?

00:10:04.879 --> 00:10:08.599
Because God has fulfilled his part

00:10:08.599 --> 00:10:11.339
in giving to us the word of God.

00:10:12.339 --> 00:10:15.559
As we consider and as we move into

00:10:15.559 --> 00:10:17.599
through the message this morning,

00:10:17.599 --> 00:10:21.039
as we consider that thought from Jeremiah 4 verse 22,

00:10:21.039 --> 00:10:23.559
the indictment against the people of Judah

00:10:23.559 --> 00:10:26.339
that to do good they have no knowledge,

00:10:26.339 --> 00:10:29.719
it's not because God didn't give them the word.

00:10:30.619 --> 00:10:32.579
God had given them the word.

00:10:32.579 --> 00:10:34.659
God had raised up prophets.

00:10:34.659 --> 00:10:37.799
We can read, it's preserved for us

00:10:37.799 --> 00:10:39.079
in the canon of scripture.

00:10:39.079 --> 00:10:42.479
We can read of the prophets of God

00:10:42.479 --> 00:10:46.499
who came and faithfully proclaimed the word of God

00:10:46.499 --> 00:10:48.239
to the people of Judah.

00:10:48.239 --> 00:10:49.739
It wasn't that they didn't,

00:10:49.739 --> 00:10:51.439
when God says that they had no knowledge,

00:10:51.439 --> 00:10:54.599
it wasn't because God had not provided it to them.

00:10:54.599 --> 00:10:57.059
It's because they didn't wanna hear it.

00:10:57.059 --> 00:10:58.259
They didn't wanna follow it.

00:10:58.299 --> 00:10:59.739
They didn't wanna know it.

00:10:59.739 --> 00:11:02.099
And so we find here that God,

00:11:02.099 --> 00:11:05.019
as we look at this passage, this verse of scripture,

00:11:05.019 --> 00:11:06.779
and we think about where it says

00:11:06.779 --> 00:11:11.779
to him that knoweth to do good, how do we know?

00:11:11.779 --> 00:11:13.899
Simple illustration this morning.

00:11:13.899 --> 00:11:16.899
If you're giving someone instructions,

00:11:16.899 --> 00:11:19.299
if you tell somebody to go do something

00:11:19.299 --> 00:11:20.699
and maybe you just leave it at that.

00:11:20.699 --> 00:11:21.839
Hey, go take care of this

00:11:21.839 --> 00:11:23.659
and you provide them with no details.

00:11:23.659 --> 00:11:25.099
And then they come, you come in there

00:11:25.099 --> 00:11:27.499
and you're just like, you did it wrong.

00:11:27.499 --> 00:11:28.619
You did it wrong.

00:11:28.619 --> 00:11:30.419
So what do you mean I did it wrong?

00:11:30.419 --> 00:11:31.399
You said to move this stuff.

00:11:31.399 --> 00:11:33.839
Yeah, but I didn't want it moved there.

00:11:33.839 --> 00:11:35.539
Well, you just said to move it.

00:11:35.539 --> 00:11:37.739
That's kind of, have you ever been in that situation?

00:11:37.739 --> 00:11:40.979
It's annoying to be in that situation, right?

00:11:40.979 --> 00:11:44.399
But we find that God has given to us.

00:11:44.399 --> 00:11:45.939
It's not that we're ignorant.

00:11:45.939 --> 00:11:48.219
It's not that we don't know what's good.

00:11:48.219 --> 00:11:50.179
It's that oftentimes we don't submit

00:11:50.179 --> 00:11:52.659
to what God has told us is good.

00:11:52.659 --> 00:11:57.459
We don't actually take and apply the truth in our lives.

00:11:58.299 --> 00:12:00.379
So if I'm gonna walk over to the room next door

00:12:00.379 --> 00:12:02.819
and say, hey, here's what I'd like to see happen.

00:12:02.819 --> 00:12:04.299
All of this stuff that's right here,

00:12:04.299 --> 00:12:05.779
I need that all to be moved

00:12:05.779 --> 00:12:07.119
and here's where we need to stage it

00:12:07.119 --> 00:12:08.779
because here's what's taking place

00:12:08.779 --> 00:12:11.299
and I provide detailed instructions

00:12:11.299 --> 00:12:14.739
and then I walk away and I come back and it's not done.

00:12:14.739 --> 00:12:17.339
Then there's a level of accountability.

00:12:17.339 --> 00:12:18.679
Does that make sense?

00:12:18.679 --> 00:12:21.019
Because the instruction has been given.

00:12:21.019 --> 00:12:24.179
The instruction has been communicated

00:12:24.179 --> 00:12:26.019
and it's been given clearly.

00:12:26.019 --> 00:12:29.219
Oftentimes when you're dealing with children,

00:12:29.219 --> 00:12:32.539
you might do as I did when we were raising our children.

00:12:32.539 --> 00:12:34.459
I would give instruction and Brother Kevin,

00:12:34.459 --> 00:12:35.619
I'd say something like this.

00:12:35.619 --> 00:12:36.719
Do you understand?

00:12:39.659 --> 00:12:40.939
Why did I do that?

